  "limitations": [
    "Static unweighted indexed meshes only; no moving/deforming meshes, texture-alpha collision masks, separate movement/weapon-query channels or finite-radius projectile sweeps.",
    "Front-face physics contacts and two-sided rays; open shells do not become closed solids.",
    "Finite-precision BVH with source and scaled-coordinate guards. No exact-arithmetic or arbitrary narrow-feature guarantee.",
    "Each body currently cooks a BVH during preparation; persistent collision cache, shared shape optimization and representative performance qualification remain unfinished.",
    "C# ray queries share accurate geometry but the current managed ABI does not expose triangle ordinal.",
    "Synthetic GUI semantic actions are not physical input, accessibility or game-feel qualification. GPU checks are one laptop with AMD integrated and NVIDIA RTX 4070 Laptop graphics, not broad hardware or game-scale performance qualification.",
    "MeshCollider data in authored worlds and internal rollback do not implement public game-save serialization."
  ],
  "resolved_findings": [
    "Export validation now catches geometry collapsing or merging at scaled float precision before backend construction; Jolt may additionally reject BVH quantization collapse.",
    "An authored diagonal is not a reliable exact tie after BVH quantization. The test now uses strict interior overlap for equal-fraction ordering and separately checks near-diagonal hits.",
    "Fresh desktop-enabled installation initially failed export because it included an SDK header. Opt-in Development installation fixed the package boundary; actual exports were rerun."
  ]
}
